  "notes": "A saltbox house 11 m wide by 10 m deep, two storeys at the front with five windows across the upper floor, a short steep front slope to a ridge 2 m back and a long rear slope falling 2 in per 1 to a lean-to eave at 2.75 m, with a central brick chimney. Faces local -Z: centred door, stair hall, a room each side of the chimney, a kitchen lean-to under the rear roof and an attic reached by a stair from the west upper room; carves nothing.",
